        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="metals" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="This module is applicable, if batch zinc coating of semifinished steel products, that's shape doesn't change anymore, has to be balanced. Data given per tonne of coated product had to be transformed dividing it by the mean surface area of 60 m2/t.  For the chemicals and the zinc, 100 km of 32t lorry transport were balanced. The softened industrial water is assumed to be produced at the coating plant. The coating layer is 65um thick, if the surface is coated on both sides and 130 um thick, if coating is done on one side only. Due to the fact, that data are given per square meter and not per kg, the energy inventoried for heavy pieces is to low and for light pieces to high. If the data would have been given per kg, the error would have been the contrary.;&#10;Synonyms: hot dip coating, galvanising; &#10;UUID: 887baada-b40f-39b4-b4f1-63f03606e790" includedProcesses="Includes the process steps degreasing, pickling, fluxing, galvanising (melt zinc coating) and finishing. Does not include the fabricates being coated." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="metals" localName="Zinc coating, pieces" localSubCategory="coating" name="Zinc coating, pieces" subCategory="coating" unit="m2"/>
